{
  "_comment": "Scale profiles. Chosen once per project (itq.mjs scale set <name>). stages: skip | lite | full per stage key. A skipped stage is stored as approved+skipped, so ordering and the hooks need no special case. rules relax checkStage; anything not listed stays strict (full has no relaxations). score: off | gates | full (off: approve needs only `check`; gates: approve needs a score round whose gates pass; full: gates plus weighted score and judges). bundles: stages the user approves together on one combined card. envelope: planning targets for one product (model minutes, USD, approvals asked of the user), set from the pilots in pilot2/ (food-bank Vision, itqan 0.7.0, wall-clock: prototype 10 min $1.98, demo 24 min $4.65, mvp 116 min $18.89) with about 1.5x margin; the full scale: cost from the v0.5-v0.6 pilots, minutes are a planning guess (those pilots timed rounds that waited on subagents too short). scaleNote: the built app must show its scale (a lite app is never mistaken for a finished product).",
  "version": 1,
  "default": "full",
  "order": [
    "prototype",
    "demo",
    "mvp",
    "full"
  ],
  "profiles": {
    "prototype": {
      "label": "Prototype",
      "for": "Test an idea or show one flow. Runs on your machine, one main path, throwaway data.",
